      "text": "Heuristic/overgeneralization: 'docker compose always restarts failed containers' assumes a restart policy is actually enabled and applies universally. Restart behavior is conditional on compose configuration; without `restart: always`/`on-failure`, no restart occurs.",
      "layer": "L3"
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "text": "Heuristic: 'restarting the container' is treated as equivalent to 'self-healing.' A restart only recreates the process; it does not fix the underlying fault (bug, bad config, dependency failure).",
      "layer": "L3"
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "text": "Conclusion with confidence ceiling: 'our backend is self-healing' has LOW to MODERATE confidence. We can be confident the container restarts after failure (if a policy is set), but not that the backend heals itself — a persistent fault causes crash-loops, not recovery.",
      "layer": "L4"
    },
    {
      "id": "F6",
      "text": "Unsupported/counter-case: a backend that exits with an error on every boot is restarted endlessly but is never healthy — direct evidence that restart ≠ self-healing. The unconditional 'always' claim is falsified when no restart policy is configured.",
      "layer": "L5"
    }
  ],
